4 TEXT Obituary 17 NOV 1921 The Centre Democrat newspaper    ASKEY - On Saturday, Nov. 5, the people of Snow Shoe were saddened by the death of Mrs. Robert Askey, who had been a sufferer from Neuritis for over a year. Two months ago she was taken to th
5 CONC e Clearfield Hospital in the hope that something might be done to relieve her suffering, but after several weeks of intense suffering, the end came.     Mrs. Askey was born in Pine Glen, Oct.29, 1857, being the oldest daughter of Jefferson and Sus
5 CONC an Force.     Almost fifty years ago, she was united in marriage to Robert Askey.     To this union eleven children were born, nine of which are living: Mrs. William Steele, Bellefonte; Jefferson Askey, Sinnemahoning; Mrs. William Long, Duluth, Mi
5 CONC nn., Mrs. Loyd Wertz, Erie; Rudolph Askey of Pine Glen; Mrs. D.W. Berkey of Beaverdale; Mrs. Edmund Rooke, Philadelphia; and Ruth, Rhoda and Sherman at home. Besides her husband, she is survived by six sisters and one brother.     Mrs. Askey wa
5 CONC s a sincere christian woman and her many deeds of kindness and love to those about her will always be a living memorial.     She was laid to rest in the Messiah Cemetery (Pine Glen) at 2:30 Wednesday afternoon. The following named men were pallbea
5 CONC rers: Curtin Askey, Loyd Wertz, Webb Berkey, Wm. Steele, Paul Mulhollan and Elmer Bowes
