4 TEXT Raymond "Pete" Poorman 76, of McClure RD1 died at Lewistown Hospital Wednesday at 6 pm. He was born in Centre County July 20, 1900, a son of the late Mitchell and Mary Jane Crock Poorman. He was twice married by his first wife the former Naomi Sto
5 CONC ver and survived by his second wife the former Beatrice M Smith. Also surviving are one son Kenneth S of State College, the following step children Mrs Eleanor Hoy of State College, Mrs Evelyn Bowersox and Mrs Patricia McCann of Pottstown, Jame
5 CONC s F Henry of McClure, Marlin D Henry and Mrs Kay Goss both of McClure, Mrs Janet Armstrong of McClure, 6 brothers Merrill Poorman, John Poorman, Toner Poorman, Daniel Poorman and Willis M Poorman all of State College and Orvis Poorman of Parma,Ohi
5 CONC o a sister Mrs Edith Spicer of Niagara Falls, New York, 19 grandchildren and 13 great grandchildren. He had been employed on the University farms. More recently he worked as a truck driver for O W Houts and sons and owned and operated a farm in Fe
5 CONC rguson Township. He retired in 1959. Funeral services will be held at Hellers Burnham Funeral Home, Burnham, Saturday at 1:30pm with the Rev McClelland Fortney officiating. Burial will be made in the Pine Hall Cemetery, State College. Friends wil
5 CONC l be received at the funeral home Friday from 7 to 9 pm.  --Centre Daily Times, Thursday Dec 30,1976
