1 EVEN JAMES ETSON McFARLAND OBITUARY  	J E. McFarland, son of Mrs. John McFarland, was born near Syracuse on September 27, 1880, and died at Kansas City on Saturday, October 3, 1914.   	Mr. McFarland was married to Miss Vergie Dillon at Nebraska City i
2 CONC n the summer of 1905.  He is survived by his wife and little son Dean, his mother and two brothers, William of Syracuse, and John of Los Angeles, Calif. 			 	His body was brought here for burial on Monday morning and the funeral was held on Tuesda
2 CONC y afternoon from his mother’s home on Tuesday afternoon at 2 o’clock.  Rev. M. P. Stiffler, of the Methodist church conducted the services.  The interment was made in Park Hill Cemetery beside his father.    Syracuse Journal, 9 October 1914, pag
