4 TEXT WWI, WWII, and Korean War Casualty Listings about Jack Pryer Williams  Name:  Jack Pryer Williams  Birth Date:  14 May 1916  Birth City:  Franklin  State Registered:  Pennsylvania  Death Date:  27 Jun 1952  Death Country:  Korea  Death Description
5 CONC :  Killed in Action   War:  Korean War  Title:  Lieutenant Colonel, U.S. Air Force  Rank:  Lieutenant Colonel  Service:  U.S. Air Force  Service ID:  7053A  Notes:  Lieutenant Colonel Williams was the pilot of a RF-86A Sabrejet reconnaissance airc
5 CONC raft with the 15th Tactical Reconnaissance Squadron, 67th Tactical Reconnaissance Wing. On June 27, 1952, while on a combat mission, his aircraft received a direct hit by anti-aircraft fire, crashed and exploded. He was not able to bailout success
5 CONC fully. Lieutenant Colonel Williams was awarded the Purple Heart, the Korean Service Medal, the United Nations Service Medal, the National Defense Service Medal, the Korean Presidential Unit Citation and the Republic of Korea War Service Medal.  Da
5 CONC ta Source:  Korean War Veterans Honor Roll
