4 TEXT Is shown on July the 28th, and the First Call, July 31, 1777, with David Anderson as 1st Lieut., Richard Coulter as 2 Lieut., William Elder, Ensign, all under Col. James Dunlap.  Col. Askey&amp;apos;s service was from 1777 to 1782 being shown on g
5 CONC uard at Frankstown, Apr, 1781.  He was from Fannet Twp,, and signed various petitions from there.  Capt. Askey mar. Elizabeth, dau. of Col. Robert Baker, June 12, 1764, the marriage by Rev. J. C. Bucher.  He was born 1727, dies 1807, his wife dyin
5 CONC g in 1830.  They are buried in an old Presby., church yard in Centre, Co., Penna. 6 miles east of Bellefonte, at Jacksonville. They had issue: John mar. Betty Evans; Wm. mar. Mary Baker; David mar. Jane Harrison; Robert mar. Mary Polly Evans; Jame
5 CONC s mar Jane Swanzey; Samual mar. Lettie McKibben; Ann mar. Baptist Lucas; Rececca mar. Joseph Lucas; Peggy mar. David Tipton; Polly unmarried.
