1 CONT OBIT:
1 CONT MRS. ASKEY, 92, OLD RESIDENT OF DAKOTA, IS DEAD
1 CONT HAD LIVED IN STEPHENSON COUNTY 80 YEARS; FUNERAL SERVICES THURSDAY
1 CONT (Special to Journal-Standard)
1 CONT Dakota, Ill., Feb 7.-- Mrs. Elizabeth B. Askey, widow of the late William Askey, and a resident of Stephenson county for 50 years, passed away at her home here last night, about 8 o'clock at the age of 92 years. Her passing came after an illness e
1 CONC xtending over the past week. It resulting from old age and a general breaking down.
1 CONT Funeral services will be conducted at 1:30 o'clock Thursday afternoon at Dakota Community church. Rev. J. Naly will conduct the services and burial will be made in the Dakota cemetery.
1 CONT Elizabeth Brenizer was born at Wooster, Ohio, on May 9, 1836. The family moved west when she was a young girl settling in Stephenson county. She was united in marriage to William Askey in 1861. The husband passed away in 1908. For the last 64 year
1 CONC s Mrs. Askey had resided in Dakota. She was well and favorably known throughout this vicinity.
1 CONT She was the last of a family of thirteen children. She is survived by two daughters they being Mrs. W. W. Diemer and Miss Bertha Askey, both of Dakota.
1 CONT (Freeport Journal-Standard, Tuesday, 07 February 1928, Freeport, Illinois)
1 CONT
