1 CONT Kansas, USA
1 CONT
1 CONT CLIFF ASKINS
1 CONT
1 CONT Cliff Askins, 52, of Girard, died at 3:10 A.M., Tuesday, October 16, 2007, in the Mt. Carmel Regional Medical Center in Pittsburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was born December 11, 1954 in Wichita, a son of Cleo and Esther (Hudson) Askins. He attended schools in Pittsburg and graduated from Pittsburg State University with a Masters Degree in History. He attended Bible college in Minot, North Dakot
1 CONC a . He taught English in China for 1 year.
1 CONT
1 CONT He served in the US Marines from 1982 until 1986.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a Christian and he provided care for his mother.
1 CONT
1 CONT Survivors include his mother of the home; a brother, David Askins of Girard; a sister, Maxine Garner of Girard; nephews Eddie Garner and his wife Leslie, Greg Garner, and Kurt Garner; great-nephews Brayden and Trevin and great-nieces Taylor, Kelse
1 CONC y, Trinity, and Emalee.
1 CONT
1 CONT Funeral services will be at 10:30 A.M., Thursday at the Girard Cemetery with Rev. Ken Sommerfeldt officiating.
1 CONT
1 CONT Friends are asked to meet at the cemetery. Memorials are suggested to the First Baptist Church in Girard or to "Angels Among Us".
1 CONT * * * * * *
