1 CONT
1 CONT James Stewart Askins Jr., 80, resident of Menno-Haven, Chambersburg, formerly of Shippensburg, died Mar. 3, 2004, in the home. Born June 28, 1923, in Harrisburg, Dauphin County to the late James Stewart Sr. and Nellie G. Stine Askins. He was a ret
1 CONC ired Social Studies teacher in Shippensburg School District. Mr. Askins was a graduate of Shippensburg University. He was a member of the Shippensburg Presbyterian Church. He was a United States Army veteran of World War II. He was a member of th
1 CONC e Cumberland Valley Lodge #315, Free and Accepted Masons, Shippensburg, Shippensburg Scottish Rite Club and the Tall Cedars of Lebanon, Valley Forest #145. He was a life member of the Durff-Kuhn VFW Post #6168, a member of the Oscar M. Hykes Ameri
1 CONC can Legion Post # 223, Lions Club, all in Shippensburg, a member of the B.P.O.E Lodge #600, Chambersburg, and a member of the Pennsylvania Association of School Retirees. Surviving are: two nephews, Joel Stewart Hoffman of Grantville & Richard Ear
1 CONC l Hoffman of Indiana, and a brother-in-law, Clye C. Morrow of Harrisburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT Burial:
1 CONT Spring Hill Cemetery
1 CONT Shippensburg
1 CONT Cumberland County
1 CONT Pennsylvania, USA
