1 CONT OBIT:
1 CONT Dakota Pioneer Dead.
1 CONT William Askey, a former station agent, died at his home in Dakota Sunday afternoon at 3 o'clock. The funeral will be held Tuesday afternoon at 1:30 o'clock from the Presbyterian church at Dakota. The Rev. Mr. Holloway will officiate.
1 CONT Mr. Askey was born May 1, 1837, in Center county, Pa. He leaves a wife and two daughters. Mrs. W. W. Deemer and Miss Bertha Askey, of Dakota. Also three grand-children and two brothers, the latter being Samuel Askey of Red Oak, and Jas. Askey, o
1 CONC f Rock Grove.
1 CONT (The Daily Journal - Monday, 06 April 1908, Freeport, Illinois)
1 CONT
1 CONT WILLIAM ASKEY, druggist, Dakota; born in Center Co., Penn., May 1, 1837 ; came to Stephenson Co., Ill., in 1849; he has an extensive and somewhat varied experience in professional and business pursuits; for the years 1865-67 and 1872-73, he was co
1 CONC nnected as teacher with Cole's Commercial College, in Peoria; in the interval between the dates above given, he was agent and operator on the Chicago .& Alton Eailroad ; in the spring of 1873, he engaged in his present business in Dakota ; haa bee
1 CONC n located here since, and is thoroughly identified with the town, his business, property and home all being here. He was married in 1861, to Miss Elizabeth Brenizer, a native of Wooster, Ohio ; their children are Ella, Jennie, Mary and Bertha.
1 CONT (The History of Stephenson County, Illinois - M H. Tilden - 1880)
1 CONT
