1 CONC ASKEY, Raymond Duane, D.V.M., June 4, 1931 - January 1, 2006, 74, passed away on January 1, 2006 in Austin, Texas. He was born on June 4, 1931 to Tom and Mary Askey in Leoti, Kansas. He attended grade school in Illinois, Indiana, and Leoti, Kansas
1 CONC , and graduated from high school in Leoti. He farmed for ten years in Western Kansas before beginning college in Houston, Texas. Ray graduated from Kansas State University in 1965. He practiced large animal veterinary medicine in Arlington, Sout
1 CONC h Dakota from 1965 until 1983 and then relocated to Chamberlain, South Dakota where he owned the Corvis Creek Veterinary Clinic until 1991. Ray served on numerous community boards as well as on the South Dakota Board of Veterinary Examiners. Afte
1 CONC r moving to Tucson, Arizona in 1991, he began the Jayhawk Mobile Veterinary Service which he continued until the time of his death. Ray was preceded in death by his parents. He will be sadly missed by his loving wife, Clare Jane, Austin, Texas; fo
1 CONC ur children, Kari Driscoll (Donn), Amber Askey, Meg Rosenquist (Kurt), all of Tucson, Arizona, and Travis Askey (Wendy), Austin, Texas; three grandchildren, Sean and Zach Driscoll, Tucson, Arizona and Jessica Askey, Austin, Texas; two sisters, Jea
1 CONC n Drushel (Harold), Wimberley, Texas and Jeanette Elder, Garden City, Kansas; numerous other relatives and a host of friends. "Doc Askey" loved his veterinary work and fulfilled his greatest wish in avoiding retirement entirely. His family was upp
1 CONC ermost in his priorities and they will miss his distinctive laugh and gentle spirit. After a private family viewing, his cremains will be placed according to his wishes. Arrangements under the care of Cook-Walden/Forest Oaks Funeral Home, 6300 W
1 CONC . William Cannon Drive, Austin, Texas, 78749, (512) 892-1172.
