1 CONT Obituary
1 CONT Paul Dolton Askins, 83, of Frontenac, passed away at 5:58 P.M. Saturday, November 21, 2009 at the Mt. Carmel Regional Medical Center. He was born July 9, 1926 at Pittsburg, to Merle LeRoy and Etta (Morgan) Askins. He attended local schools and gra
1 CONC duated from Pittsburg High School in 1944.
1 CONT
1 CONT Mr. Askins served in the United States Navy during World War II from 1944 to 1946. He married Lois Allen on December 30, 1945 in Pittsburg. She preceded him in death. On November 11, 1998, he married Birdie Nell Burr in Pittsburg. She survives hi
1 CONC m at the family home.
1 CONT
1 CONT Mr. Askins worked for Meadow Gold Dairy, A.J. Cripe Bakery and Askins Construction, where he bought and fixed up rental properties. Membership was held in the Frontenac United Methodist Church, Benjamin Fuller American Legion Post No. 64, where h
1 CONC e was a member for 60 years.
1 CONT
1 CONT In addition to his wife, he is survived by a son, Dr. Dale Askins and his wife, Dana of Oklahoma City, OK; a daughter, Sandy Post and her husband, Greg of Mapleton, KS; a sister, Lucretia "Doll" Lightkep of Salt Springs, FL; four grandkids, Todd V
1 CONC an Gorden and wife, Amy, Traci Vincent and husband, Doug, Lindsey Megahee and husband, Jason, and Kelly McCaskill and husband, Jeff; five great-grandkids, Johnathon Vincent, Nicholas Vincent, Emily McCaskill, Reid McCaskill, and Dolton Megahee; an
1 CONC d numerous nieces and nephews.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents, two brothers, Merle and Tommy Askins, and a sister, Edna Mae Hall. Services will be 10:30 a.m. Tuesday (November 24) at the Brenner Mortuary, with Rev. Dennis Paschke officiating. Burial will follow in Gard
1 CONC en of Memories, where the Benjamin Fuller American Legion Post No. 64 will provide flag folding ceremonies.
1 CONT
1 CONT The family received friends from 6:30 p.m. to 8:00 p.m. Monday at the Brenner Mortuary. The family suggests memorials to the Frontenac United Methodist Church or the American Heart Association. These may be left at or mailed to the Brenner Mortuar
1 CONC y, 114 E. 4th St., Pittsburg, KS 66762. Online condolences may be left at www.brennermortuary.com. Arrangements are under the direction of the Brenner Mortuary, Pittsburg, KS.
1 CONT
1 CONT Membership was held in the Frontenac United Methodist Church, Benjamin Fuller American Legion Post No. 64, where he was a member for 60 years.
1 CONT
1 CONT The Morning Sun
1 CONT Posted Nov 23, 2009 @ 10:38 PM
1 CONT
