1 CONT Vancouver, WA
1 CONT
1 CONT A graveside service will begin at 2 p.m. Monday at Park Hill Cemetery in Vancouver for Gertrude Askay, 89, who died on Friday, March 28, 1997, in Vancouver.
1 CONT
1 CONT Mrs. Askay was born April 8, 1907, in Griggs, N.D., and had been a Vancouver resident for the last 66 years. She worked as a nurses aid for 30 years in Clark County, and was a member of the Retired Hospital Employees of Vancouver. She was also a m
1 CONC ember of the Senior Citizens Group of Vancouver.
1 CONT
1 CONT Mrs. Askay was preceded in death by her husband, Joe, who died in 1949; a daughter, Irene, who died in 1982; and a grandson, Dan French, who died in 1989. Survivors include one son, Robert of Vancouver; three daughters, Eva Mae Tingley of Vancouve
1 CONC r, Joan Blaisdell of Carson, and Betty Buttner of Longview; one brother, Alfred Gammelgard of Nenomonee, Wis.; seven grandchildren; and nine great-grandchildren.
1 CONT
