1 CONC Birth: Mar. 23, 1855
1 CONT New Bloomfield
1 CONT Perry County
1 CONT Pennsylvania, USA
1 CONT Death: Aug. 28, 1909
1 CONT New Bloomfield
1 CONT Perry County
1 CONT Pennsylvania, USA
1 CONT
1 CONT After weeks of terrible suffering, death came as a blessed relief to Mrs. Willis K. Clouser, at her home, one mile north of this place, in Centre Twp. at her home. She was afflicted with cancer of the liver and for more that a year had been confin
1 CONC ed to the house and was bedfast for the past month.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jane Elizabeth Clouser was a daughter of the late William H. and Margaret Ann (Stone) Askins, of this place (New Bloomfield). She was born March 23, 1855, and was married in 1873, to Willis K. Clouser by Rev. A.H. Aughe, of Newport. They had eleve
1 CONC n children, seven of whom are dead, five of dying of diphtheria within a three week period in 1890. This terrible affliction so broke down the health of Mrs. Clouser that she was never well thereafter. The surviving children are; Misses Annie an
1 CONC d Louise and Charles and Cyrus. She is also survived by the following brothers; W.H., Harry C. and Charles W. Askins, and one half sister, Mrs. W.H. Copp, all of this place, and the following step-brothers and step-sisters; John A. Angney, of Oa
1 CONC k Grove; Mrs. C.W. Smith, of Newport; Mrs. Mary Grove of Hummelstown; and Mrs. Emma Smith, of Harrisburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT When only fourteen years of age the deceased united with the Reformed Church and was a constant member all her life thereafter. She was a good, kind wife and mother and will be sadly missed in the home circle. To the bereaved husband and childre
1 CONC n we extend our sincere sympathy.
1 CONT
1 CONT The funeral was on Monday with Rev. J. Thomas Fox officiating. Interment was in the New Bloomfield Cemetery. The pallbearers were her four nephews; Ross Clouser, and Clyde Askins, of this place, and Charles R. and Lynn D. Clouser, of Newport. Sh
1 CONC e was aged 54 years, 5 months, and 5 days.
1 CONT
1 CONT [Perry County Democrat. September 1, 1909]
