1 CONC Chester C. Askey
1 CONT
1 CONT UNIONTOWN Chester "Chet" Clyde Askey, of Uniontown, Ohio, was born in Por tage, Pa., on July 14, 1922, to Perry and Rebecca Askey.
1 CONT
1 CONT Chet served three years in the South Pacific during World War II as Seaman First Class. He worked at General Tire for 39 years, retiring in April of 1979.
1 CONT
1 CONT He is survived by loving wife of 58 years, Elva (nee Wilson); daughters, Leslie (Larry) Krause of Santa Paula, Calif., Betty Jo (Richard) Houck of Silver Lake; grandchildren, Lauren and Spencer Houck; brother-in-law, Jack (Bertie Lou) Wilson; neph
1 CONC ew, Paul Askey; and niece, Gloria Bays.
1 CONT
1 CONT Cremation has taken place. A memorial service will be at a later date. (Adams-Mason, 330-535-9186.)
1 CONT
1 CONT Published in the Akron Beacon Journal from 6/19/2004 - 6/20/2004.
