0 @N60@ NOTE
1 CONC Alfred's parents are David Earl and Rachel Couteret. My grandfather Alfred Askey was married to Rose Massaro and my dad is David J Askey my mom is Audrey Drake. I have a copy of the original Askey-Gross family tree which is so intersting and wonde
1 CONC rful to look bak at. As a child my siblings and I spent fun Labor Day and Memorial Day weekends in PA visiting all my grandfathers relatives. I remember meeting many people We would go to a reunion every year right near the the Askey Cemetary an
1 CONC d we enjoyed reading the stones (a little wierd?) and playing in the old church. It was a great "history" lesson.... One of the most memorable people was introduced to me as Uncle Roy. He was about 90 years old and still hunted racoon. He showed u
1 CONC s his barn where he hung all the hides. We also played with his 2 hound dogs. I am thinking it was Ralph Roy Askey. Quite an adventure for a child that lived in the suburbs of NYC. We also met Aunt Helen in the pocono's she was almost completely b
1 CONC lind from cateracts I think? But she crocheted the most wonderful things. All her rugs in her home were made by her. And she gave us crocheted dolls to take home.
