1 CONT MOSES FRAME BUCHANAN OBITUARY
1 CONT
1 CONT DEATH OF AGE SETTLER
1 CONT
1 CONT After an illness of more than twelve years, being bedfast nearly all the time, suffering from paralysis Mose F. Buchanan died last night at his home three miles northwest of this city. He was born June 9, 1849 in Ohio, and came to Nebraska City i
1 CONC n 1873, and has since made his home in this vicinity. He was married here to Jennie M. Davis, May 1, 1895, and is survived by the following children - Glen M., Martha G. And James M. Buchanan, all of this city. In the earlier days he was quite wel
1 CONC l known. He was a gentleman whom it was a pleasure to know and had many friends.
1 CONT He was a member of the Methodist church. The funeral will be Sunday afternoon at 2:30 o'clock at the Free Methodist church corner of Eighth street and First avenue. The cortege will leave the family home at 2 o'clock sharp. The interment will be a
1 CONC t Wyuka.
1 CONT
1 CONT Nebraska City News, 13 Aug 1918, p.3
