1 CONC Birth: 	Oct. 19, 1923
1 CONT Fulton Run
1 CONT Indiana County
1 CONT Pennsylvania, USA
1 CONT Death: 	Jan. 18, 2012
1 CONT Mansfield
1 CONT Richland County
1 CONT Ohio, USA
1 CONT
1 CONT Frank William Askey, 88, of Ashland died Wednesday, Jan. 18, 2012, at MedCentral Hospitals.
1 CONT
1 CONT Frank was born Oct. 19, 1923, in Fulton Run, Pa., the son of Thomas S. and Rose E. (née Merinka) Askey.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a 1942 graduate of Ashland High School. Frank enlisted in the Navy, transferring to the Marines, serving in the South Pacific during World War II.
1 CONT
1 CONT Former Dominion, Glenn Roofing employee, Frank retired from F.E. Myers in 1985. He served on the Myers Employee Recreation Association, Myers Credit Union as recording secretary, the shop committee for LL1297, and was a delegate to Ohio State Coun
1 CONC cil of Machinist, District 54 and Central Labor. He also served on United Appeals Board.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a member of Ashland Nazarene Church and also attended Grace Brethren Church. He was a lifetime member of VFW Post 1067, Ashland Senior Citizens and McDonald's breakfast bunch.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Jane Askey, on June 19, 1976, who survives.
1 CONT
1 CONT In addition to his wife, Frank will be deeply missed by his daughters, Pat (Mike) Marker and Ruth (Phil) Shafer, both of Ashland; one son, David Askey of Tombstone, Ariz.; four grandsons, Michael and Mark Marker, William (Val) Shafer and Christoph
1 CONC er Askey; eight great-grandchildren, Amber, Mary, Markie, and Megan Marker, Mallory, Josh and Hannah Marker, Zane Shafer and Chris Askey; and five great-great-grandchildren, Jaylyn, Caleb, Ryleigh, Raiden and Bethany; longtime family friends, Char
1 CONC lotte and Ron Elson; two stepchildren, Larry Stroub of Polk and Lois (Wayne) Rameau of Fitchburg, Mass.; two stepgrandsons, Mike (Wendy) Stroub of Nankin and his brother and sister, Levi and Tiffany (Cody Gibbons) Elson, Wade Wolf (Janette Brown
1 CONC ) of Elyria; four stepgreat-grandchildren, Jordan, Zack, Nate, and Trevor Stroub of Nankin; a great-great-granddaughter, Cayliegh Elson of Ashland.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents; two brothers, Robert and Marvin; one great-grandchild; and his first wife, Harriette Miller.
1 CONT
1 CONT Funeral services will take place 1 p.m. Saturday, Jan. 21, 2012, at Roberts Funeral Home, Ashland Chapel, 1058 U.S. 250 N., with Pastor Norm Johnson and the Rev. Beatty officiating. Visitation will take place 5 to 7 p.m. today, Jan. 20, 2012, at t
1 CONC he funeral home. Interment will be in Ashland County Memorial Park. Military rites will be presented by the Joint Veterans Association.
1 CONT
1 CONT Memorial contributions may be made to the Checkered Pantry c/o Ashland Veterinary Clinic, 626 E. Main St., Ashland, Ohio 44805; or to the donor's choice.
1 CONT
1 CONT Online tributes may be made on the funeral home's website at www.robertsfuneralhome.com. (T-G 01/20/12)
1 CONT
1 CONT Note: U.S. Navy & Marine Corp, World War II Veteran
1 CONT
