1 CONT
1 CONT Zola Baumann, 67, passed away Friday, Nov. 30, 2012, with her family by her side, at Samaritan Evergreen Hospice House.
1 CONT A celebration of life will take place on Saturday, Dec. 15, in the multipurpose room of Philomath Elementary School. Please stop by any time between 4 and 6 p.m. to visit with friends and family.
1 CONT Zola was born July 19, 1945, to Milo and Murial Askay (both preceded her in death). Her father was a deputy sheriff and mechanic in Philomath. Her mother worked at Oregon State University. They moved to Philomath in 1949, where Zola remained livin
1 CONC g till the end of her life.
1 CONT Zola graduated from Philomath High School in 1963. After graduation, she remained in Philomath and married James Baumann (later divorced) and raised their four daughters.
1 CONT She started her banking career at First National/First Interstate in Philomath and later transferred to First Interstate/Wells Fargo in Corvallis. After retiring from Wells Fargo, she worked as a book-keeper/payroll specialist for Tax and Wealth M
1 CONC anagement, and was working for the Philomath Youth Activities Club at the time of her death.
1 CONT She devoted much of her time and energy to her daughters' families, watching her children and grandchildren in all their activities. In particular, Zola spent many years sitting on a bleacher, rain or shine, supporting and cheering on her family f
1 CONC or all types of activities. In her downtime, she enjoyed quilting, knitting, reading and spending time with family and friends at their beach getaways.
1 CONT Zola is survived by her brother, Milo Askay of Belleview, Fla.; four daughters and their spouses, Teresa (Mark) Preddy of Philomath, Tina (Ken) Blanscet of Parma, Idaho, Traci (Norm) Hammond of Tillamook, and Tara (Dan) Bevandich of Philomath; an
1 CONC d nine grandchildren, James Laramee, Steven, Rebecca, Paul and Deborah Blanscet, Ryan and Kaylin Hammond, and Matthew and Alixandra Bevandich.
1 CONT
