1 CONT Death:  Nov. 29, 2010
1 CONT Prince Frederick
1 CONT Calvert County
1 CONT Maryland, USA
1 CONT
1 CONT Lee Raymond Minin, 79, of Solomons, Md., formerly of Alexandria, Va., died Monday, Nov. 29, 2010, in Prince Frederick, Md.
1 CONT Born April 4, 1931, in Franklin, he was the son of the late Emma Jane Borland and John Abraham Minin.
1 CONT Lee married Lorraine Post which ended in divorce. After his divorce he married his beloved wife, April Minin, in Queens Village, N.Y.
1 CONT Lee graduated in 1949 from Franklin High School and went on to graduate from Tri State College in Angola, Ind. in 1952.
1 CONT Lee began his career working for Goodyear Aerospace in Akron, Ohio, as an electrical design engineer on Navy blimps. He then became the support contractor for SUBROC, continuing to work on that program as a NAVSEA employee. As he advanced in his c
1 CONC areer he became the deputy program manager and was instrumental in the success of HARPOON, the Norwegian Penguin Weapon System and the release, operation, and support of the Tomahawk Missile. His profound efforts have contributed greatly to our na
1 CONC tional security over his many years in federal service. He retired in 2006 after 38 years of service.
1 CONT Lee belonged to the Sons of the American Legion, NARFE, St. Paul United Methodist Church, and the Academy of Model Aeronautics. His favorite hobby was radio controlled model airplanes.
1 CONT In addition to his parents, Lee was preceded in death by his siblings, Virginia and Jackie Minin.
1 CONT Lee is survived by his wife April Minin of Solomons, Md; his children, John Minin of Sugarland, Texas, Kenneth Minin of Cabot, Ariz. , Ronald Minin of Spring, Texas, and Jennifer Minin of Solomons, Md.; seven grandchildren; and two great grandchil
1 CONC dren.
1 CONT
1 CONT The family will receive friends from 2 to 4 and 6 to 8 p.m today in the Rausch Funeral Home Chapel, Lusby, Md.
1 CONT Funeral services will be held at 11 a.m. Thursday in St. Paul United Methodist Church, Lusby, Md., with the Rev. Ron Collier officiating.
1 CONT Interment will be at 11a.m. Saturday in Franklin Cemetery, Franklin.
1 CONT Huff Chapel Inc., 312 West Park St. Franklin, is in charge of local arrangements.
1 CONT The Derrick - December 1, 2010
1 CONT
