2 TITL Thomas Aspy/Askey - Emigrants In Bondage (Transportation to Colonies)
2 _DATE Apr 1742
2 _TEXT Record of the sentence and transportation in bondage of Thomas Aspy/Askey to the American Colonies.     Sentenced in 1741, Aspy/Askey landed in the New World in April of 1742 on the convict ship Philleroy.    Per the UK National Archives, from 161
3 CONC 5 onwards transportation became increasingly common, and initially most people were transported to North America or the West Indies. From 1718 onwards transportation was entirely to North America. The period of transportation was usually 14 year
3 CONC s for those receiving conditional pardons from death sentences and seven years for non-capital offences.        Philleroy mentions:    http://books.google.com/books?id=Hd4XAQAAIAAJ&pg=RA1-PA199&lpg=RA1-PA199&dq=ship+philleroy&source=bl&ots=aYVYpVn
3 CONC 3li&sig=zlMGfUFdA1yRZFR32ON71sp8too&hl=en&sa=X&ei=DSEeT87pFtTYiAKA2pnDCw&ved=0CCAQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=ship%20philleroy&f=false         Name: Thomas Aspy  Year: 1742  Place: Maryland  Source Publication Code: 1236.50  Primary Immigrant: Aspy, Thoma
3 CONC s  Annotation: Date of sentencing to transportation and intended destination or date and place of arrival. Where sentenced, reason for sentencing, name of ship, where record found, and other information may be provided. Information extracted fro
3 CONC m central criminal records (Midland Circuit Criminal Process Book 1739-1742, ASSI 12/2; Sheriffs' Cravings, E197, E 389, T64/262, and T90/146-160; State Papers (Criminal), SP44/79-83), county records, printed journals (Brist  Source Bibliography
3 CONC : COLDHAM, PETER WILSON. More Emigrants in Bondage: 1614-1775. Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co., 2002. 217p.  Page: 5      Sheriffs' Cravings aka Bills of Sheriffs' Cravings. These are sheriffs' bills of cravings, that is, annual claims fo
3 CONC r reimbursement of money spent during their official engagements, such as magistrates' wages, judges' lodgings, courtroom furniture, messengers' payments, conveyance of criminals to trial, burning or whipping some of them and 'dieting' others unti
3 CONC l they were transported.
